 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "I wish I would.",
   "texto": [
    "**-(으)면 좋겠어요** expresa que el hablante desea que se cumpla una situación: 날씨가 **좋으면 좋겠어요** (ojalá haga buen tiempo), 합격하면 좋겠어요 (ojalá apruebe). Desire may refer to the person who speaks or to another person, depending on the context."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Distinguish condition and desire",
   "texto": [
    "**-(으)면** followed by another action poses a condition: **날씨가 좋으면 공원에 가요** = if it's a good time, we go to the park. **-(으)면 좋겠어요** adds the wish: **날씨가 좋으면 좋겠어요** = I wish it would make good weather. To wish for an action you want to do, it is also common **-았/었으면 좋겠어요**; it is enough to recognize it for now:"
   ]
